@startuml State - User Lifecycle
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam state {
    BackgroundColor #E3F2FD
    BorderColor #1565C0
    ArrowColor #1565C0
    StartColor #1565C0
    EndColor #B71C1C
    FontSize 12
}
skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #FFF8E1
    BorderColor #F9A825
}
skinparam shadowing false

title User Account — Lifecycle State Diagram

[*] --> Unregistered : (initial state)

Unregistered --> PendingVerification : POST /users\n(Cognito sign_up + DynamoDB put_item)\nstatus 201

PendingVerification --> PendingVerification : POST /users/verify\n(wrong code / expired code)\nstatus 400

PendingVerification --> Verified : POST /users/verify\n(confirm_sign_up OK)\nDynamoDB: email_verified=true\nstatus 200

PendingVerification --> Unregistered : DynamoDB write error\n(Cognito admin_delete_user ROLLBACK)\nstatus 500

Verified --> LoggedIn : POST /users/login\n(initiate_auth OK)\nstatus 200 + tokens

LoggedIn --> LoggedIn : GET /users\nGET /users/{userid}\nstatus 200

LoggedIn --> LoggedIn : PUT /users/{userid}\n(owner only)\nstatus 200

LoggedIn --> Forbidden : PUT or DELETE\nby another user\nstatus 403

Forbidden --> LoggedIn : (returns to normal flow)

LoggedIn --> Deleted : DELETE /users/{userid}\n(owner only)\nstatus 200

LoggedIn --> Unregistered : token expired /\nno longer authenticated

Deleted --> [*]

note right of PendingVerification
  Cognito sends a
  verification email
  automatically after sign_up
end note

note right of LoggedIn
  Tokens:
  IdToken (1 hour)
  AccessToken (1 hour)
  RefreshToken (30 days)
end note

note right of Forbidden
  Ownership rule:
  caller_sub must equal userid
  for PUT and DELETE
end note

@enduml
